From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: PS5: call the syscall dispatcher at 0x7ffe4000

ps5-forever-wine ee64b784 (bizkut/ps5-forever, deps.json pin
d465aa69e0625f57591634e1a0ffe753c329d13f1f7c089b2d39dafd12761453)
builds the x64 Nt* thunk as Wine's form and names the dispatcher
0x7ffe4000, the next 16 KiB host page after KUSER_SHARED_DATA.
SystemCall stays 1, so the thunk's 0f 05 is not executed. int 2e is
not part of that stub.

The stock PE still has call [0x7ffe1000]. After the signal handlers
exist, and only when anon_mmap_fixed(0x7ffe4000, 0x4000) returns that
address, each immediate 00 10 fe 7f becomes 00 40 fe 7f. A Win10 tail
is put back on that call. A failed map leaves call [0x7ffe1000].
The per-thread int 2e emulator stays for a fault that still executes
those bytes. The stub repair accepts both dispatcher addresses.

wine_ps5_title_game_image from the same commit recognizes a
drive-qualified Wow*.exe when a sibling <stem>_loader.dll exists, then
a lowercase basename (Wow.exe -> wow_loader.dll, WowB.exe stays
WowB_loader.dll, WoWClassic.exe -> WowClassic_loader.dll). Their
game_launch is not present here, so NtCreateUserProcess logs the leaf
and continues the helper spawn. The predicate lives in
wine/ps5/pw_wow_loader.h. No console run.
---
--- a/include/wine/asm.h
+++ b/include/wine/asm.h
@@ -283,7 +283,17 @@
  * Windows. For 64-bit systems the only viable form we can emulate is
  * having an int $0x2e fallback. Since actually using an interrupt is
  * expensive, and since for some reason Chromium doesn't actually
- * validate that instruction, we can just put a jmp there instead. */
+ * validate that instruction, we can just put a jmp there instead.
+ * On PS5 the dispatcher pointer sits at 0x7ffe4000, the first 16 KiB
+ * boundary past the user shared data at 0x7ffe0000, rather than at
+ * 0x7ffe1000: 0x7ffe1000 shares the shared data's host page and cannot
+ * be mapped on its own (dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c). From
+ * bizkut/ps5-forever-wine ee64b784 include/wine/asm.h. */
+# if defined(__WINE_PS5__) || defined(__PROSPERO__)
+#  define __ASM_SYSCALL_DISPATCHER_ADDR ".long 0x7ffe4000\n\t"
+# else
+#  define __ASM_SYSCALL_DISPATCHER_ADDR ".long 0x7ffe1000\n\t"
+# endif
 # define __ASM_SYSCALL_FUNC(id,name) \
     __ASM_GLOBAL_FUNC( name, \
                        __ASM_SEH(".seh_endprologue\n\t") \
@@ -296,8 +306,8 @@
                        ".byte 0xc3\n\t"           /* 14: ret */ \
                        ".byte 0xeb,0x01\n\t"      /* 15: jmp 18 */ \
                        ".byte 0xc3\n\t"           /* 17: ret */ \
-                       ".byte 0xff,0x14,0x25\n\t" /* 18: callq *(0x7ffe1000) */ \
-                       ".long 0x7ffe1000\n\t" \
+                       ".byte 0xff,0x14,0x25\n\t" /* 18: callq *dispatcher */ \
+                       __ASM_SYSCALL_DISPATCHER_ADDR \
                        ".byte 0xc3" )             /* 1f: ret */
 #elif defined __arm__
 # define __ASM_SYSCALL_FUNC(id,name,args) \
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -2282,8 +2282,9 @@
     load_ntdll_functions( module );
 #if defined(__PROSPERO__) && defined(__x86_64__)
     /* Count the Win10 thunks and leave call [0x7ffe1000] in place.
-     * signal_init_process rewrites the tail to int 2e after the handlers
-     * exist. SystemCall stays 1: a Windows syscall number enters the kernel. */
+     * signal_init_process retargets that immediate to 0x7ffe4000 after the
+     * handlers exist. SystemCall stays 1: a Windows syscall number enters
+     * the kernel. int 2e is not installed. */
     ps5_arm_ntdll_syscalls( module );
 #endif
     if (is_arm64ec()) redirect_ntdll_functions( module );
